### 2. POSTMORTEM WIRING: ISOLATED ISLAND (NOT GATED)

**Search command proving absence of postmortem as prerequisite:**
```bash
rg "postmortem.*required|raise.*postmortem|postmortem.*gate" /home/marielle/projects/bathos/src/bathos --type py
# No results — postmortem is never raised as an error or gate requirement
```

**Call sites of postmortem functions across src/bathos/ (excluding postmortem.py):**

- `cli.py`: Three commands (`scaffold`, `show`, `validate`) in `postmortem_app` — all CLI-only, optional, user-driven (lines annotated in earlier read)
- `repair.py`: Counts postmortem annotations for warm-DB rebuild warning (line 150: "postmortem_count=0" default; line 189-190: advisory only, does not gate rebuild)
- `schema.py`: Fields stored in Run dataclass (defaults: "unassigned", "none", "" — line 239-248)
- `compact.py`: Migration v3→v4 sets all postmortem fields to defaults (line 287-297)
- `query.py`: Deserializes postmortem columns from warm DB (lines 283-290)
- `rich_fmt.py`: Renders postmortem panel only if status != "unassigned" (line 159-167; purely display, no gate)
- `cli.py` compact/check/run/submit: No postmortem checks or requirements

**VERDICT:** Postmortem is an **isolated, read-only annotation surface**. It is never required by `bth run`, `bth submit`, `bth campaign conclude`, `bth check`, `bth lint`, or `bth sprint-audit`. All postmortem fields default to inert values ("unassigned", "none", ""). Postmortem cannot gate any workflow.

